From 326d0466c7a0d860e863f6abe8dcbb2f86509c17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:25:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/47] NMXAccel: order VM-display flips on NMXPublished >=
 NMXPending, not the lock seed

The first ordered flips waited for the surface's IOSurface lock seed to
move. That seed moves when a write lock is TAKEN (before the copy), and
CoreDisplay takes write locks of its own, so flips went out before the
pixels: frames showed out of order and scrolling glitched. A trace also
showed every frame takes two command buffers into the same surface
(WindowServer's composite, then CoreDisplay's AccessComplete pass), so the
second one landed in the surface already on the panel.

Now the plugin sets surface values: NMXPending at commit of each command
buffer writing the surface, NMXPublished after its copy-out; the flip waits
until NMXPublished >= NMXPending (read with IOSurface::copyValue), cap
100 ms. Such flips are NMX_SCANOUT_FINAL; timed-out ones are not.
Counters: nmxfb_front_written (frames published into the surface on the
panel; 93% of flips before, 0 now), debug.nmxfb_ord_trace=N logs N flips.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
